{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap","requirement":"A landlord may not demand or receive security exceeding one month's rent, in addition to first month's rent. Small landlords owning no more than two properties with four units may charge up to two months' rent. Advance payment of six months' rent is allowed for leases of six months or longer.","key_value":"1 month's rent (2 months for small landlords)","coverage_conditions":"Residential property used as the tenant's dwelling. Small landlord exception applies to natural persons or LLCs with all natural-person members owning no more than two residential rental properties with four total dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Residential property used as tenant's dwelling"},"exemptions":"Security collected before July 1, 2024; advance payment of six months' rent if lease term is six months or longer; service member higher security rules.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"Except as provided in paragraph (2), (3), or (5), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to one month’s rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Service member higher security deposit disclosure and return","requirement":"On or after April 1, 2025, a landlord charging a service member higher than standard security based on credit history or similar factors must provide a written statement explaining the higher amount before lease signing, and must return the additional amount after no more than six months of residency if the tenant is not in arrears.","key_value":"Return additional security after 6 months","coverage_conditions":"Service members who rent residential property where they will reside.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Service members"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"On or after April 1, 2025, if a landlord or its agent charges a service member who rents residential property in which the service member will reside a higher than standard or advertised security pursuant to paragraph (1) due to the credit history, credit score, housing history, or other factor related to the tenant, the landlord shall provide the tenant with a written statement","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Limits on security deposit deductions","requirement":"A landlord may not claim against the tenant or the security for preexisting damages, ordinary wear and tear, or the cumulative effects of ordinary wear and tear occurring during one or more tenancies.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies governed by this section.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancies"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"The landlord shall not assert a claim against the tenant or the security for damages to the premises or any defective conditions that preexisted the tenancy, for ordinary wear and tear or the effects thereof, whether the wear and tear preexisted the tenancy or occurred during the tenancy, or for the cumulative effects of ordinary wear and tear occurring during any one or more tenancies.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Initial inspection of rental unit before move-out","requirement":"Within a reasonable time after notice of intent to terminate, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the option to request an initial inspection and the right to be present. If requested, the landlord must conduct an inspection before final inspection and give at least 48 hours' prior written notice.","key_value":"48 hours' notice","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies under this section, unless terminated for certain eviction causes.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancies"},"exemptions":"Tenancies terminated pursuant to subdivision (2), (3), or (4) of Section 1161 of the Code of Civil Procedure.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"Within a reasonable time after notification of either party’s intention to terminate the tenancy, or before the end of the lease term, the landlord shall notify the tenant in writing of the tenant’s option to request an initial inspection and of the tenant’s right to be present at the inspection.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Photographic documentation of rental unit condition","requirement":"Beginning April 1, 2025, a landlord must take photographs within a reasonable time after the unit is returned and before any repairs or cleanings deducted from the security, and must take photographs before or at the inception of a tenancy beginning on or after July 1, 2025.","key_value":"Photographs before and after tenancy","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies under this section.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancies"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"Beginning April 1, 2025, the landlord shall take photographs of the unit within a reasonable time after the possession of the unit is returned to the landlord, but prior to any repairs or cleanings for which the landlord will make a deduction from or claim against the security deposit pursuant to this section, and shall also take photographs of the unit within a reasonable time after such repairs or cleanings are completed.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":true,"conflict_note":"Subdivision (g)(1) also requires photographs at inception for tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025."}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and itemization","requirement":"No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant vacates, the landlord must furnish an itemized statement and return any remaining security. If the landlord in bad faith fails to comply, the landlord may not claim any amount of the security.","key_value":"21 calendar days","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies under this section.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancies"},"exemptions":"Deductions for repairs and cleaning together not exceeding $125; tenant waiver signed after termination notice.","penalty":"Landlord shall not be entitled to claim any amount of the security if the landlord, in bad faith, fails to comply with this subdivision.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"No later than 21 calendar days after the tenant has vacated the premises, but not earlier than the time that either the landlord or the tenant provides a notice to terminate the tenancy under Section 1946 or 1946.1, Section 1161 of the Code of Civil Procedure, or not earlier than 60 calendar days prior to the expiration of a fixed-term lease, the landlord shall furnish the tenant, a copy of an itemized statement","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Transfer of security deposit upon change of ownership","requirement":"Upon termination of the landlord's interest in the premises, the landlord or agent must, within a reasonable time, either transfer the remaining security to the successor in interest and notify the tenant, or return it to the tenant with an accounting.","key_value":"Reasonable time","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies under this section when the landlord's interest terminates by sale, assignment, death, appointment of receiver, or otherwise.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential tenancies"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Successors in interest jointly and severally liable for repayment of the security if landlord fails to comply.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"Upon termination of the landlord’s interest in the premises, whether by sale, assignment, death, appointment of receiver, or otherwise, the landlord or the landlord’s agent shall, within a reasonable time, do one of the following acts, either of which shall relieve the landlord of further liability with respect to the security held:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
